        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 474,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 424,
        "paragraph_id": "1615AC5A",
        "text": "Both formulations make use of the wave-averaged turbulence energy (ks) and a mixing length (Lmix). The wave averaged turbulence energy at the surface is computed from the roller energy dissipation and following Battjes (1975) in which Dr is roller dissipation:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 17838,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 478,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 428,
        "paragraph_id": "19723C85",
        "text": "The mixing length (Lmix) is expressed as thickness of the surface roller near the water surface and depends on the roller volume Ar (Svendsen, 1984):"
